Run `pwd` and confirm with the user that it is the connected project folder; if not, `cd` to it in every command. Step 5 then runs `config.py init --project`, which also writes `.gtm/.gitignore` so `credentials.json` never reaches git.
   - In the home folder, `~/.config/gtm` (the default in Claude Code). Step 5 runs `config.py init`.
   On a re-run, `config.py paths` shows the active folder (`source`, `dir`). Keep it unless the user asks to move.
@@ with
Run `pwd` and confirm with the user that it is the connected project folder; if not, `cd` to it in every command. Step 5 then writes `.gtm/config.json` and `.gtm/.gitignore` (with the line `credentials.json`, so a key of Tessary GTM Pro never reaches git).
   - In the home folder, `~/.config/gtm` (the default in Claude Code). Step 5 writes `~/.config/gtm/config.json`.
   On a re-run, the folder command (`config.md`, No Python, step 1) shows the active folder. Keep it unless the user asks to move.
